cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this synchronized revision snapshot, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Dynamic Risk Mitigation in Edge Computing: A Queuing-Theoretic Framework for Reliability-Important Cascading Failure Prevention"
abstract: >
  A queue-motivated reliability-control framework integrating a proxy-informed
  load-dependent hazard model with graph-aware continuous control (GAT-SAC) for
  cascading-failure mitigation in edge computing networks. The synchronized revision
  snapshot bundles the canonical BA-100 paired benchmark, fixed-policy hazard-slope
  replay, topology-transfer probes, and illustrative OVHcloud replay artifacts.
